   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Fisheye video \u2192 per-frame splats \u2192 .splat4d\n\nEvery frame becomes its own 3D splat cloud; a video depth model\n(Video-Depth-Anything, metric) keeps geometry consistent across frames, and\nWAN 2.1 VACE fills the background that is never revealed behind moving\nobjects.\n\n**Stages**\n1. **VideoMetricDepthEstimate** \u2014 temporally consistent metric depth (needs\n   the Video-Depth-Anything repo at the ComfyUI root and\n   `metric_video_depth_anything_vitl.pth` in models/checkpoints).\n2. **TemporalStaticPlate** \u2014 static/dynamic split from temporal median color\n   AND depth deviation; closing fills body interiors; background hidden\n   behind movers is completed from deepest-depth observations. Its\n   `unobserved_mask` marks background nobody ever saw.\n   \u26a0 open/close/dilate radii are in pixels \u2014 scale them with resolution\n   (defaults here are tuned for 2048\u00b2).\n3. **WAN VACE disocclusion fill (render space)** \u2014 the novel-view splat\n   render + its inverted coverage mask go through WanVaceToVideo: WAN fills\n   exactly the pixels no splat covered (disocclusions, hair fringes),\n   temporally consistently. Inpainting the fisheye directly does NOT work \u2014\n   WAN warps wide-angle geometry \u2014 so the fill happens on pinhole renders.\n   Models: wan2.1_vace_14B_fp16, umt5_xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled, wan_2.1_vae.\n4. **SplatFramesFromVideo** \u2014 per-frame splats: shared static base + per-frame\n   dynamic splats; constant count & pixel-identity order; depth-edge\n   'flying pixels' suppressed (resolution-independent threshold).\n5. **RenderSplatSequence** \u2014 novel-trajectory render + fisheye replay.\n5b. **BakeRenderFill** \u2014 unprojects the WAN-filled hole pixels (depth\n   continued from the surrounding rendered background) into the STATIC\n   splat layer \u2192 the exported .splat4d handles occlusions itself.\n   Check the `novel_baked` WEBM: raw render of the baked scene.\n6. **SaveSplats4DVideo** \u2014 antimatter15 .splat frames \u2192 one streamable\n   .splat4d (pip install splats4d; viewer in the splats4D repo).\n\n**Previews**: depth video, motion-mask video, novel WEBM (raw + WAN-filled), replay WEBM.\n\n**Tune**: color/depth thresholds & close_radius (mask coverage),\nedge_threshold (silhouette streaks), splat_scale (pinholes vs blur),\nstride (splat count), WAN prompt (describe the empty scene!)."
   ],
   "title": "About this workflow"
  },
